refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;

 resourcefalsestream_socket_accept
 resourcesocket
 floatnulltimeout&null;
 stringpeer_name&null;



 Accept a connection on a socket previously created by
 stream_socket_server.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.2.0

     Now throws a ValueError if
     timeout is not a finite value.




    8.0.0

     timeout is now nullable.

&reftitle.notes;
This function should not be used with UDP server sockets. Instead, use stream_socket_recvfrom and stream_socket_sendto.
With an ssl:// or tls:// server, the TLS handshake runs inside the call. It is bounded by the timeout of the listening stream (see stream_set_timeout), not by the timeout argument: a client that stays silent keeps the call blocked for the timeout of the listening stream, which then emits E_WARNING messages and returns &false;.
